Export _dma_cache_wback and _dma_cache_inv for assembling the WiFi driver module.

In arch/mips/mm/cache.c, of the three DMA operation pointers, only
_dma_cache_wback_inv. Driver rtl8192cd uses all three (rings of descriptors
TX/RX on the incoherent DMA), so when assembled by MODULE modpost stops the assembly:

  ERROR: "_dma_cache_wback" [drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8192cd/rtl8192cd.ko] undefined!
  ERROR: "_dma_cache_inv"   [drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8192cd/rtl8192cd.ko] undefined!

Patch 900-realtek-dma-operation.patch from the fork openwrt-AC10, rebuilt according to the reference
tree 4.14.275; the context in 4.14 is the same as in 3.18.

The built-in Ethernet driver does not need these exports because it links directly into the
kernel. The rtl8192cd driver is a loadable module, so modpost must see both symbols exported
before it can produce rtl8192cd.ko.

This patch was regenerated against the Linux 4.14.275 reference tree rather than edited by
hand, keeping its context aligned with the pinned kernel revision.

--- a/arch/mips/mm/cache.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/cache.c
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@
 void (*_dma_cache_inv)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
 
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(_dma_cache_wback_inv);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(_dma_cache_wback);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(_dma_cache_inv);
 
 #endif /* CONFIG_DMA_NONCOHERENT || CONFIG_DMA_MAYBE_COHERENT */
 
